Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset: transparent strategy-game squad attack sprite sheet. Input image is the EDIT TARGET, the existing 5-column by 2-row ten-frame attack atlas. Revise its gun-arm poses to make a clear, physical raise -> aim straight ahead -> fire -> recoil -> return attack. KEEP the same painted style, individual unit identities, original detailed clothing and weapons, five-man squad in each cell, exactly two rear soldiers and three front soldiers, and exact fixed overhead crown-down 90-degree orthographic camera. All units face SCREEN BOTTOM. This request is about animating arms and the orientation of held guns, not redesigning the characters. LOCK head centres, squad spacing and scale, cell pivots and silhouettes between frames. Make the held barrel direction visibly DIFFERENT from diagonal low idle carry. In the AIM and FIRE poses, all five guns point FORWARD toward the bottom edge, their bore axes VERTICAL DOWN in the image within 5 degrees, not diagonally sideways across the body. Guns are raised horizontally parallel to the ground, not pointed into the ground or toward the camera. All members including ALL THREE FRONT SOLDIERS must visibly raise and aim, not only the back pair. Genuine transparent alpha; no background, floor, shadow, grid, labels, watermarks or text. Output WIDE 5:2 atlas, five equal square cells per row, two rows, ten complete squads. Each squad completely isolated inside its own cell, generous transparent gutters and room for smoke, no clipping or crossing cell boundaries.
Animation frame order left to right top row then bottom row:
1 same low diagonal ready carry as original first frame, no smoke;
2 halfway transition, all gun arms lift forward, elbows open, muzzles rotate from diagonal carry toward straight down;
3 fully AIMED FORWARD, stock firmly braced, arms holding aimed gun at shoulder height, all five barrels VERTICAL DOWN and visible forward, no flash or smoke;
4 same held fully aimed pose, no smoke, this is a distinct aiming beat BEFORE firing;
5 FIRE from the exact same forward aimed orientation, tiny bright yellow-white muzzle flashes and compact soft grey-white smoke puffs emanating ONLY at all five actual barrel ends. Recoil braced visibly;
6 slight recoil at shoulder while all five guns still point downscreen FORWARD, expanded soft white-grey smoke floating ahead in continuation of the five muzzle axes;
7 smoke thins and drifts forward, guns remain shouldered and continuous;
8 arms begin lowering to ready, faint smoke wisps fade out;
9 low carry ready same as first frame, no smoke;
10 low carry ready same as first frame, no smoke.
Do not just add smoke to the old idle pose. Preserve ONE continuous, hand-held gun per man in EVERY frame, no disappearing guns, weapon swapping, extra barrels, detached wrists, barrels through arms or bodies.
Exactly five short broad-bore wooden-stock infantry firearms. Preserve the short thick dark-steel barrels, brass muzzle bands and brown wooden full stocks, not long muskets. Stock butts nest at viewerLEFT shoulder, trigger wrist remains viewerLEFT and support hand grips WOOD fore-end farther down the barrel axis. To aim ahead they turn and lift the complete guns from diagonal down-right carry to vertical down, extend their support arm ahead of the chest, shoulder the butt, lean subtly into the shot. The support hand supports wood beneath the barrel and does not grip the steel muzzle. Give the front middle BLUE-coated red-feather man a complete unmistakable forward aim before shooting, same as all others. Keep red/blue coats, cream cuffs, brown gloves and belts, morions and feathered brown hats exactly as source. All muzzles project forward out of the troop's shoulders, not concealed at the waist.

